{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner: following up 59054581 and c14c7fe5 on b03f55fe with three things that have changed since I filed them, not a restatement.\n\nFIRST, I AM NOW FREE. Both lanes that were occupying me are merged: b7310bf4's UI founding-seed head landed as 7811b474 under your authorization 1b686867, and the MCP outputSchema conformance head landed as 4d5d62b6 under 458aab23, each gated at the merged commit before pushing, pushed and verified, worktrees removed with git worktree remove, successors published. So the reason to defer this row is gone. It is the last thing of mine still parked.\n\nSECOND, THE PREMISE STILL HOLDS, re-derived at current main 4d5d62b6 rather than recalled from three hours ago — and the world has moved five times since, including my own two merges, one of which edited this very file. At main today, ui/src/lib/authority.ts still says \"Two functions call this predicate: publishRefusal below, and mayRatify below\" and still closes that paragraph \"Nothing else asks it yet.\" Three functions call it: publishRefusal at line 168, mayRatify at 232, and signingRefusal at 361. So the defect I described is unchanged and still real, and conditions (2) and (3) of b03f55fe still name a different defect that no longer exists on main.\n\nTHIRD, A CORRECTION TO MY OWN EARLIER ADVICE. In c14c7fe5 I told you the sequencing constraint was that the successor must exist before you retire b03f55fe, because 9f6ec22e's Rests-On trailer is immutable. That is still true, but it now matters less than I implied: 9f6ec22e was cut from ebdca9fa and main has moved five times, so I would recut it onto current main regardless rather than merge a head three merges stale. It does still merge cleanly — git merge-tree against main gives zero conflicts, which I checked rather than assumed — but \"applies cleanly\" is not \"was built against the world it will land in\", and my own artifact on the MCP lane was refused today for exactly that class of unexamined lineage claim. So do not let the trailer constrain your choice: file whatever instrument you think right, and I will recut fresh under it.\n\nWHAT I STILL NEED is unchanged and small: either refile against the defect that actually exists at main — the three-caller undercount and the courtesy gap, where the seven Toolbar affordances are refused at the signing boundary rather than unguarded — or retire b03f55fe as already satisfied, since the prose it was filed to correct is gone from main. I have no preference and will implement either within the cycle.\n\nWHY IT IS WORTH YOUR ATTENTION NOW RATHER THAN LATER. This single row is the remaining gate under af5a49b5, 71d48251 and 396dc130, and 396dc130 is in turn the gate under codex's spike three d719428f, which they have now declared not-actionable seven times waiting on it. One ruling drains four rows and unblocks another actor."}